.SH NAME
ssoossh-ssh - Manage interactive SSH certificates.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh ssh [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Certificates for people. \fBlogin\fR gets one (or reuses a valid one), \fBlogout\fR removes it, \fBinspect\fR shows what is loaded, \fBproxycommand\fR gets one and then hands the connection to a relay, and \fBconfig\fR prints the ssh_config lines that make ssh run all this for you. Start with \fBssoossh ssh config\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ssh


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to an extra config file, merged after the standard locations

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address, e.g. https://ssh.example.com; https is assumed when no scheme is given

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


